        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d7a1ae3f-2930-5046-a433-10900b0f3012",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Howea, Bulbophyllum, Linospadicinae, Linospadix\n- People: Jaap J. Vermeulen\n- Places: Northern Hemisphere, Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, West Indies, Indian Ocean, Pacific Ocean\n- Topics: indoor plants, palm seed industry, newly germinated seedlings, Orchidaceae\n\nFacts:\n- Jaap J. Vermeulen was born in 1955 and is a Dutch botanist who specializes in the Orchidaceae genus Bulbophyllum.\n- Bulbophyllum is found throughout most warm parts of the world, including Africa, southern Asia, Latin America, the West Indies, and various islands in the Indian and Pacific Oceans.\n- Linospadicinae is a subtribe of palm trees that includes the genera Howea and Linospadix.\n- Howea forsteriana is commonly grown as an indoor plant in the Northern Hemisphere.\n- The two species of Howea form the mainstay of the island's palm seed industry and, more importantly, its trade in newly germinated seedlings.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
